{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Arrogant</b> — like גבר יהיר (an arrogant man), that is, a scoffer who acts proudly." "<b>His name is 'scoffer'</b> — And our Rabbis of blessed memory said: Once he became haughty over them through transgression — that is, he transgressed to act presumptuously — and the transgression hints at anger that passed and overpowered the faculty of will, in the manner of עברו ראשי (my head passed) when sins grow strong."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "The phrase עברו ראשי is cited tersely without a source; rendered hyper-literally as Ibn Ezra quotes it. The reading רז\"ל resolved as 'our Rabbis of blessed memory' by standard convention."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:04.997167559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}